Third-party attribution
-----------------------

Portions of this project are ported from, or implemented with reference
to, source files of the MAME project (https://www.mamedev.org/). Each
of those upstream files is individually licensed under the same BSD
3-Clause terms as above, with copyright held by its authors, and those
portions remain under their authors' copyright:

Ported code and data tables:

  - src/devices/machine/steppers.cpp
      copyright-holders: James Wallace
      (stepper phase maps and update logic in src/hw/reel.ts)
  - src/mame/bfm/bfm_bd1.cpp
      copyright-holders: James Wallace
      (BD1 character set table in web/bd1font.ts)
  - src/mame/barcrest/mpu4_characteriser_pal.h
      copyright-holders: David Haywood, James Wallace
      (per-game characteriser tables in src/machine/mpu4chr.ts)
  - src/mame/bfm/bfm_comn.cpp
      copyright-holders: David Haywood
      (Scorpion 2 ROM descramble tables in src/machine/sc2.ts)
  - src/devices/video/roc10937.cpp
      copyright-holders: James Wallace
      (16-segment charset and cursor LUT in src/hw/s16lf01.ts; also the
      protocol model for src/hw/msc1937.ts)
  - src/devices/sound/upd7759.cpp
      copyright-holders: Juergen Buchmueller, Mike Balfour, Howie Cohen,
      Olivier Galibert, Aaron Giles
      (ADPCM state machine, timings and step tables in src/hw/upd7759.ts)
  - src/devices/sound/saa1099.cpp
      copyright-holders: Juergen Buchmueller, Manuel Abadia
      (register decode, update loop, envelope and amplitude tables and
      noise generator in src/hw/saa1099.ts)
  - src/mame/bfm/sc4.cpp and src/mame/jpm/jpmimpctsw.cpp
      copyright-holders: David Haywood
      (ROM identification tables in tools/sc4-crcs.json and
      tools/impact-crcs.json)

Behavioural reference (hardware behaviour, address maps, protocols):

  - src/mame/barcrest/mpu4.cpp
      copyright-holders: David Haywood, James Wallace
  - src/mame/bfm/bfm_sc2.cpp
      copyright-holders: James Wallace
  - src/mame/bfm/bfm_sc4.cpp
      copyright-holders: David Haywood
  - src/mame/jpm/jpmimpct.cpp
      copyright-holders: Philip Bennett, David Haywood
  - src/devices/cpu/m6809/m6809.cpp
      copyright-holders: Nathan Woods
  - src/devices/machine/i8255.cpp
      copyright-holders: Curt Coder
  - src/devices/machine/mc68681.cpp
      copyright-holders: Mariusz Wojcieszek, R. Belmont, Joseph Zatarski
  - src/devices/sound/ymz280b.cpp
      copyright-holders: Aaron Giles

The .fml layout decryption scheme implemented in web/fml.ts was
recovered by John Parker (johnparker007) for the Oasis project's FML
decoder; the implementation here is an independent reimplementation of
that scheme.

